# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Which parts of results/<RUN_ID>/ travel with the code.
#
# Tracked: the analysis tiers -- small, and the only thing worth comparing a
# new dataset's numbers against (40_stats, 50_costs, 60_report, and the two
# 20_benchmarks staging trees that produced them).
#
# Ignored: the bulk tiers.  10_runs alone is ~30 MB of per-seed run trees and
# 30_atombench* another ~5 MB of per-target metric dumps; both are outputs of
# a run on THIS cluster against the JARVIS Supercon-3D split, so they are dead
# weight to a clone that is about to regenerate them from a different dataset.
#
# Patterns are RUN_ID-agnostic on purpose: a new run under a new RUN_ID gets
# the same treatment without editing this file.
#
# The tree is results/<dataset>/<run id>/, one level per benchmark, so that the
# JARVIS Supercon-3D run and the Alexandria DS-A/B run cannot collide:
#
#     results/jarvis/2026-08-30_full/
#     results/alex/2026-09_alex_dsab/
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# 2026-09-06: the bulk tiers are now DVC-tracked (see the .dvc files beside
# them and the repo-root PROJECT_STATE.md); 00_provenance is small and travels
# in git.  DVC writes its own ignore entries for what it tracks.

__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
